.PP
constructs a node manifold accessing the supplied node colony and node pointers Creates a node manifold from the 2 pointers to co-located nodes\&. Additional nodes can be added to it later\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fInodes\fP reference to the primary storage of the nodes in the \fBMeshManager\fP 
.br
\fIinside\fP pointer to the node that will assumed to be on the INSIDE of the interface that that manifold is part of 
.br
\fIoutside\fP opposing yet collocated node in the manifold 
.br
\fImanifold_type\fP geometric classifier of the new manifold, default is INTERFACE but may need to be revised if the node is at a model boudary or other\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
an iterator to the new manifold stored in a colony in the \fBNodeManifoldManager\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
this method does not assign the nodes to the new manifold\&.; this must be done by calling Node::Assign( manifold ) after its successful creation which only happens on the return from this method\&. 
.RE
.PP

